      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A small thick-walled glass tube was loaded with HOmes (0.35 g, 2.6 mmol), Er metal filings (0.83 g, 5.0 mmol), and Hg (2 drops). The tube was evacuated (<10−3 mmHg), sealed, and heated in a 220 °C oven for 4 days, then cooled to ambient temperature. Pink rectangular crystals of 15 were observed interspersed with unreacted Er and mercury; an X-ray quality crystal was hand-picked in a drybox. Toluene extraction of the mixture gave a pink solution that concentrated to a pink oil.",
